<rules>
<rule id="3c67-4893-3aa1-a1e4" name="Allegiance" hidden="false">
<description>The army's Allegiance determines which characters, units, wargear, Rites of War and other options may be selected. A Legion is not inherently restricted to a particular Allegiance.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="cdd0-030c-6049-1d7f" name="Allies Matrix: Space Wolves" hidden="false">
<description>Allies Matrix - At the Height of the Heresy. Allies and Brothers: Blood Angels, Exercitus Imperialis, Imperial Fists, Iron Hands, Mechanicum, Questoris Households, Raven Guard, Salamanders, Solar Auxilia, Space Wolves, Ultramarines, White Scars. Conditional Alliance: Blackshields (The Lost and the Damned), Dark Angels, Talons of the Emperor. Sworn Enemies: Alpha Legion, Daemons of the Ruinstorm, Death Guard, Emperor's Children, Iron Warriors, Night Lords, Sons of Horus, Thousand Sons, Word Bearers, World Eaters. Apply the chart separately to every pair of detachments in the army. An alliance never overrides army-building restrictions, allegiance requirements or the specific wording of a unit, ability or item of wargear. A Legion fielded with the other allegiance (e.g. Loyalist Sons of Horus) swaps sides: Sworn Enemies that only come from the two sides of the Heresy become allies, and all detachments of an army must share one allegiance.</description>
</rule>
</rules>
